language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ hidato: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Hidato puzzles start semi-filled with numbered tiles. Connect the numbers together to win.
$ Consecutive numbers must touch horizontally, vertically, or diagonally. The numbers must be in
$ increasing order. Fill in the empty cells, marked 0 in the given puzzle, with the numbers that
$ complete the puzzle, so that the grid holds each number from 1 to the number of cells exactly
$ once.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `hidato.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/hidato.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `hidato_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py hidato.json
$   savilerow model.eprime hidato_1.param -run-solver

$ puzzle_dim1, puzzle_dim2: the number of rows and of columns of the grid (derived from the data)
given puzzle_dim1, puzzle_dim2 : int
letting nr = puzzle_dim1
letting nc = puzzle_dim2
$ nn: the number of cells; the numbers are 1 to nn
letting nn = nr * nc
$ puzzle[r,c]: the number given in row r, column c, or 0 for an empty cell (1-based)
given puzzle : matrix indexed by [int(1..nr), int(1..nc)] of int(0..nn)
$ x[r,c]: the number in row r, column c of the solved grid
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..nr), int(1..nc)] of int(1..nn)
$ at_row[k], at_col[k]: the row and the column of the cell holding the number k
find at_row : matrix indexed by [int(1..nn)] of int(1..nr)
find at_col : matrix indexed by [int(1..nn)] of int(1..nc)

such that
$ every number from 1 to nn is used exactly once
allDiff([x[r,c] | r : int(1..nr), c : int(1..nc)]),
$ the numbers given in the puzzle are kept
forAll r : int(1..nr) . forAll c : int(1..nc) . (puzzle[r,c] > 0 -> x[r,c] = puzzle[r,c]),
$ at_row and at_col say where each number is
forAll k : int(1..nn) . x[at_row[k], at_col[k]] = k,
$ the number k+1 touches the number k horizontally, vertically or diagonally
forAll k : int(1..nn-1) . (at_row[k] - at_row[k+1] <= 1 /\ at_row[k+1] - at_row[k] <= 1 /\ at_col[k] - at_col[k+1] <= 1 /\ at_col[k+1] - at_col[k] <= 1)
